  $$https://picsum.photos/seed/demo-alvaro-choque-mendoza/800/200$$,
  $$Álvaro Choque Mendoza is an agricultural engineer with twenty years of experience in irrigation and climate adaptation in the Bolivian and Peruvian Andes. He has designed and managed small irrigation systems, micro-dams and water harvesting for farming communities facing glacier retreat and erratic rainfall, and has led the irrigation components of national and donor-funded programmes. He manages multi-disciplinary teams through design, construction and handover to water user organizations, and supports the change management needed when communities shift to new water allocation rules. Álvaro speaks Aymara and works directly with community water committees. He also works on glacial flood early warning and sustainable farming with irrigation users.$$,
