  $$Abdiwali Hersi Warsame is a nutrition survey specialist who has worked across the Somali region of Ethiopia, Somaliland and south-central Somalia for nine years. He has designed and led more than twenty SMART and coverage surveys for humanitarian agencies, adapting sampling to pastoralist mobility and insecure areas and training enumerator teams in anthropometric measurement. His statistical analysis work covers wasting and stunting trends, mortality estimates and the links between drought, food security and malnutrition. He also supports nutrition programme monitoring, building dashboards that cluster coordinators and regional health bureaus use for targeting. Abdiwali works fluently in Somali, which lets him run focus groups with mothers and community health workers directly, and he is comfortable spending long periods in the field. He also works on early warning for drought and on livestock and pastoral livelihoods.$$,
  $$[{"name":"Nutrition","tier":"core"},{"name":"Survey Design","tier":"core"},{"name":"Hydromet & Early Warning","tier":"core"},{"name":"Food Security","tier":"strong"},{"name":"Statistical Analysis","tier":"strong"},{"name":"Humanitarian Response","tier":"strong"},{"name":"Monitoring & Evaluation","tier":"strong"},{"name":"Data Visualization","tier":"strong"},{"name":"Livestock & Animal Health","tier":"working"}]$$::jsonb,
